Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[N 38-40 Storm, Heed, Tempest]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\From Farholde Keep by Stormwind to Arathi: Veyric takes the twenty Twisted Totems and sends you after the Ravaging Tempest; Captain Nials's report, Illari's cache and Faldir's Cove; then Menethil, Theramore and Ratchet, down the Barrens past Razorfen Downs and through the Great Lift to the quilboar ritual in Thousand Needles.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 38: the Faldir's Cove naga are 38-40 and the ritual's Ravaging Tempest is a level 40 elite (the DB's level) with a level 38 elite quilboar beside it (GROUP 3+). Every quest here needs 30-36 (Bring the Light needs 39), so nothing is blocked; under 38, pull the cove naga one at a time and bring a group for the ritual
[OC]|cffffcc00Start:|r Farholde Keep in the Riverglades when chapter 38 is done, whatever your level (about 38); hearth = Farholde Keep and it stays there. About 19,940 quest XP and 1g 60s on the plain quests handed in here, every one of them plain; the chapter ends at the Razorfen Downs door in the far south of the Barrens (chapter 39b)
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r No Honor Among Thieves (79242) from Tokal in Booty Bay (chapter 37), handed in at Illari's cache. Shaman: Storm, Earth, and Fire (79358) with all 20 Twisted Totems (5 Water from chapter 32, 5 Air from 33, 5 Fire from 35, 5 Earth from 37), handed in at Veyric. The Coldbringer's Eye (96773, chapter 34) rides on to Razorfen Downs (39b)
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Training:|r no trainer on this trip; the level 38 and 40 ranks wait for Ironforge (chapter 39d)

[OC]|cffffffffStormwind|r  -  one stop, and only if you are level 39: Bring the Light needs 39. At 38 Benedictus has nothing for you; you may instead fly from Gretchen straight to Refuge Pointe (the game routes it through Thelsamar) and skip the three Stormwind steps. Razorfen Downs runs without Bring the Light
At [TAR257087 Gretchen Mayberry], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Stormwind]|r (Farholde Keep - Lakeshire - Stormwind; the game routes it) [G60.9,80.9 Riverglades]
[O]Only if you are level 39: in the Cathedral of Light at [TAR1284 Archbishop Benedictus], [QA3636 Bring the Light] (4,300 XP at the hand-in, requires level 39: kill Amnennar the Coldbringer, the last boss of Razorfen Downs, chapter 39b; handed in here on chapter 39d's Stormwind trip). At 38 skip it [G50.3,45.5 Stormwind City]
At [TAR352 Dungar Longdrink], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Refuge Pointe]|r (through Ironforge; the game routes it) [G71.3,72.2 Stormwind City]

[OC]|cffffffffRefuge Pointe|r  -  Captain Nials stands beside the flight master
At [TAR2700 Captain Nials], [QA95315 The Riverglades Report] (285 XP, requires level 36: Captain Nials' Correspondence goes to Demar Brant at Farholde Keep - carried to chapter 40) [G45.8,47.6 Arathi Highlands]

[OC][A Shaman]|cffffffffVeyric Thunderhame|r  -  about 24 units north-east of Refuge Pointe, as in chapter 29: approach him from the WEST. Fozruk (42 elite), the Cresting Exiles (38-39) and Myzrael (44 elite) stand east of him, and Hammerfall's Horde guards further east are level 50. Do not go past him
[A Shaman] At [TAR259023 Veyric Thunderhame], [QT79358 Storm, Earth, and Fire] (3,600 XP + 60s: the 20 Twisted Totems) [QA96135 Heed My Call] (3,150 XP at the hand-in, back at Veyric after Razorfen Downs: he gives you the Corrupted Totems to end the quilboar ritual in Thousand Needles and bring back the Eye of the Tempest) [G59.8,27.6 Arathi Highlands]

[OC]|cffffffffIllari's cache|r  -  far east on the Arathi coast, about 50 units south-east of Veyric. The DB gives only the cache, no path: keep south of Hammerfall (Horde, level 50 guards) and ride down to the shore, |cffffcc00path unverified|r
Click Illari's Loot Cache on the shore, [QT79242 No Honor Among Thieves] (3,900 XP + 1g, plus a fixed item the data does not describe) [G94.1,69.3 Arathi Highlands]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (79242):|r |cff66ff66Traveled Gloves|r (leather +9 Str, +11 spell damage) - take them if your gloves are any of the Prospector Gloves, the Ironforge Agent's Gloves or weaker (40.0 vs 31.5 / 26.3 on the level-40 weights); they also beat the Seawolf Gloves from the cove below (25.4). If chapter 38 gave you the Prisoner Handwraps (60.0), nothing here is an upgrade: take the Soldier's Visor (plate) to sell (81s 38c). Determined Band (+8 Sta, +9 attack power) is weaker than both

[OC]|cffffffffFaldir's Cove|r  -  ride back west past Refuge Pointe and south-west to the goblin camp on the south-west coast (the road south from Refuge Pointe leads there, as in chapter 29). Every quest here needs level 35. Daggerspine Raiders (38-39, 42 spawns at x17-26 y84-91) and Sorceresses (39-40, 10 spawns at x18-24 y84-90) stand on the shore west of the camp: pull them singly at 38
At [TAR2766 Lolo the Lookout], [QA663 Land Ho!] (690 XP: talk to Captain O'Breen) [G31.8,82.7 Arathi Highlands]
At [TAR2610 Shakes O'Breen], [QT663] [G32.3,81.4 Arathi Highlands]
At [TAR2769 Captain Steelgut], [QA664 Drowned Sorrows] (3,150 XP: 10 Daggerspine Raiders and 3 Daggerspine Sorceresses) [G34.0,80.8 Arathi Highlands]
|cFFFF0000ESCORT|r At [TAR2768 Professor Phizzlethorpe], [QA665 Sunken Treasure] (3,150 XP: escort him to the cave and back; he hands in to Doctor Draxlegauge beside him) [G33.9,80.5 Arathi Highlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Escort:|r the quest text says only "to the cave and back"; the path and any ambush are not in the DB (|cffffcc00unverified|r). Stay close and keep him alive
Escort [TAR2768 Professor Phizzlethorpe] to the cave and back [QC665] [G33.9,80.5 Arathi Highlands]
At [TAR2774 Doctor Draxlegauge], [QT665] [QA666 Sunken Treasure] (3,900 XP: 10 Elven Gems from the Calcified Elven Gems on the naga shore; he gives you the Goggles of Gem Hunting, which he wants back) [G33.9,80.5 Arathi Highlands]
Kill [TAR2595 Daggerspine Raider] and [TAR2596 Daggerspine Sorceress] (10 and 3) on the shore west of the camp [QC664] [G22.1,87.1 Arathi Highlands]
Wear the Goggles of Gem Hunting and loot 10 Elven Gems from the Calcified Elven Gems among the naga (23 in the DB, x18-25 y84-92) [QC666] [G22.8,88.2 Arathi Highlands]
At [TAR2769 Captain Steelgut], [QT664] (3,150 XP) - |cffffcc00Gear:|r Seawolf Gloves (leather +11 Str +3 Agi) lose to the Traveled Gloves: vendor them [G34.0,80.8 Arathi Highlands]
At [TAR2774 Doctor Draxlegauge], [QT666] (3,900 XP) [QA668 Sunken Treasure] (1,550 XP: the Elven Gems go to Captain O'Breen) - |cffffcc00Gear (choice):|r take the Servomechanic Sledgehammer to sell (vendor price 1g 48s 87c): it needs Engineering 100; the Gnomish Zapper is a wand [G33.9,80.5 Arathi Highlands]
At [TAR2610 Shakes O'Breen], [QT668] (1,550 XP) [QA669 Sunken Treasure] (3,150 XP at the hand-in: the Sample Elven Gem goes to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay, after Razorfen Downs by the Ratchet boat) [G32.3,81.4 Arathi Highlands]

[OC]|cffffffffTo Kalimdor|r  -  Refuge Pointe to Menethil, the boat to Theramore (flight point from chapter 32), then the flight to Ratchet (flight point from chapter 26)
At [TAR2835 Cedrik Prose] in Refuge Pointe, |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Menethil Harbor]|r (the game routes it) [G45.7,46.1 Arathi Highlands]
Take the boat to Theramore from the far south-west pier (the sign on the pier names the destination; Questie marks this dock "Portal To Theramore", so boat or portal is |cffffcc00unverified|r) [G5.6,63.2 Wetlands]
At [TAR4321 Baldruc] in Theramore, |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Ratchet]|r [G67.5,51.3 Dustwallow Marsh]

[OC]|cffffffffThe Barrens road|r  -  chapter 26's road: from Ratchet west to the main road, then south past the Crossroads and Camp Taurajo (Horde towns, level 40 guards: stay on the road and never stop in their yards) to the bottom of the Barrens. The DB has no road data, so the markers are chapter 26's. Ghost Wolf for the ride
Ride west from Ratchet to the main road and follow it south to Camp Taurajo (stay on the road) [G44.5,59.2 The Barrens]
Keep following the road south past the burnt tower to the bottom of the Barrens [G46.4,73.9 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffcc00Razorfen Downs:|r Myriam Moonsinger at the Downs' door (49.0,94.9) starts chapter 39b; the Downs come after the ritual, when you come back from Thousand Needles. Elite quilboar and cultists (33-34) stand around the door: give them room on the way past
Ride on past Myriam Moonsinger and the Downs to the Great Lift and take it into Thousand Needles (the DB has two Great Lift objects, at 29.2,34.2 and 43.3,46.9 Thousand Needles; the marker is the first, |cffffcc00unverified|r) [G29.2,34.2 Thousand Needles]

[OC][A Shaman]|cffffffffHeed My Call|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r. The ritual site is at 36.6,38.9 Thousand Needles: Ailgrha Splittusk <Mother of Storms> (level 38 elite quilboar), four Ravaging elementals (Storm, Quake, Flood, Drought; level 38, not elite) and the Ravaging Tempest (elite, level 40 in the DB, 6 spawn points at x36-37 y37-42). The Grimtotem and the Boiling and Scalding Elementals around it are 25-29, grey to you. The Tempest's and Ailgrha's tooltips also give a point at about 54-55,41-42: if the ritual is not at 36.6,38.9, look there (|cffffcc00unverified|r). Solo or group is untested: bring two friends or invite whoever is there
[A Shaman] |cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Use the Corrupted Totems at the ritual (10 min cooldown), kill the summoned [TAR216474 Ravaging Tempest] and loot the Eye of the Tempest (100% drop) [QC96135] [G36.6,38.9 Thousand Needles]
Take the Great Lift back and ride to Myriam Moonsinger at the Razorfen Downs door [G49.0,94.9 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r handed in here: Storm, Earth, and Fire (79358), No Honor Among Thieves (79242), Land Ho! (663), Drowned Sorrows (664) and Sunken Treasure (665, 666, 668). In the log: Heed My Call (96135) with the Eye of the Tempest (Veyric, chapter 39c), Sunken Treasure (669: Fleet Master Seahorn, Booty Bay, chapter 39c), The Riverglades Report (95315: Demar Brant, chapter 40), The Coldbringer's Eye (96773: Razorfen Downs, chapter 39b) and, if you were 39 in Stormwind, Bring the Light (3636: the Downs, 39b; Benedictus, 39d). Hearth = Farholde Keep. Next: Razorfen Downs
[NX 39-40 Razorfen Downs]
